00081184<\/p>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta answer-tag-list tags_ans_lp\"><strong>Tags<\/strong>:<a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'mingw'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">mingw<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'manual'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">manual<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'configure'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">configure<\/a><\/div>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\"><ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\"><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span>15<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span>2081<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-feedback feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span>0<\/li><\/ul><\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\"><div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\"><div class=\"answers_meta -is_accepted\" data-accepted-label=\"Accepted Answer\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"1 Accepted Answer, 2 Answers\"><span class=\"answers_meta_count\">3<\/span><span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answers<\/span><\/div><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/div>\n    <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n        <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n            <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/2184607-axes-label-in-root-locus?s_tid=ans_recom_leaf\">Axes label in root locus<\/a><\/p>\n            <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                    <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                        <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                            <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/2249004\">\n                                    <img alt=\"Anna\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"\/responsive_image\/75\/75\/0\/0\/0\/profile\/2249004?s_tid=ans_recom_user\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, '\/responsive_image\/100\/0\/0\/0\/0\/cache\/matlabcentral\/profiles\/profilepic_default.gif');\">\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                            <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/2249004\">Anna<\/a> on 11 August 2026\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                    <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\"> When I draw a root locus, the label for the axes appear as: Real Axis (seconds^-1) Imaginay Axis (seconds^-1) I&#39;d like to remove (seconds^-1). I used to have the commands: axIm = findall(gcf,&#39;String&#39;,&#39;Imaginary Axis (seconds^{-1})&#39;); axRe = findall(gcf,&#39;String&#39;,&#39;Real...<\/p>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta answer-tag-list tags_ans_lp\"><strong>Tags<\/strong>:<a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'root locus'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">root locus<\/a><\/div>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\"><ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\"><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span>0<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span>245<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-feedback feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span>2<\/li><\/ul><\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\"><div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\"><div class=\"answers_meta -is_accepted\" data-accepted-label=\"Accepted Answer\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"1 Accepted Answer, 2 Answers\"><span class=\"answers_meta_count\">3<\/span><span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answers<\/span><\/div><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/div>\n    <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n        <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n            <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/100687-how-do-i-extract-data-from-matlab-figures?s_tid=ans_recom_leaf\">How do I extract data from MATLAB figures?<\/a><\/p>\n            <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                    <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                        <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                            <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/4622813\">\n                                    <img alt=\"MathWorks Support Team\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"\/responsive_image\/75\/75\/0\/0\/0\/profile\/4622813?s_tid=ans_recom_user\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, '\/responsive_image\/100\/0\/0\/0\/0\/cache\/matlabcentral\/profiles\/profilepic_default.gif');\">\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                            <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/4622813\">MathWorks Support Team<\/a> on 10 July 2013\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                    <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\"> I have a few MATLAB figures, but no MATLAB code associated with it. I want to extract the data from the curves in the figures. kA0i00000007qGVCAY 000024646<\/p>\n                        <div class=\"search_result_meta answer-tag-list tags_ans_lp\"><strong>Tags<\/strong>:<a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'extract'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">extract<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'data'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">data<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'figure'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">figure<\/a><\/div>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\"><ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\"><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span>23<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span>573<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-feedback feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span>0<\/li><\/ul><\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\"><div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\"><div class=\"answers_meta -is_accepted\" data-accepted-label=\"Accepted Answer\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"1 Accepted Answer, 2 Answers\"><span class=\"answers_meta_count\">3<\/span><span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answers<\/span><\/div><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/div>\n    <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n        <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n            <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/100459-how-can-i-insert-a-title-over-a-group-of-subplots?s_tid=ans_recom_leaf\">How can I insert a title over a group of subplots?<\/a><\/p>\n            <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                    <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                        <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                            <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/4622813\">\n                                    <img alt=\"MathWorks Support Team\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"\/responsive_image\/75\/75\/0\/0\/0\/profile\/4622813?s_tid=ans_recom_user\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, '\/responsive_image\/100\/0\/0\/0\/0\/cache\/matlabcentral\/profiles\/profilepic_default.gif');\">\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                            <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/4622813\">MathWorks Support Team<\/a> on 26 April 2010\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                    <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\">I would like to place a title over a group of subplots. How can I do this? kA0i00000007kpBCAQ 000003742<\/p>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta answer-tag-list tags_ans_lp\"><strong>Tags<\/strong>:<a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'supertitle'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">supertitle<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'super'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">super<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'subplot'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">subplot<\/a><\/div>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\"><ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\"><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span>12<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span>560<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-feedback feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span>0<\/li><\/ul><\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\"><div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\"><div class=\"answers_meta -is_accepted\" data-accepted-label=\"Accepted Answer\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"1 Accepted Answer, 4 Answers\"><span class=\"answers_meta_count\">5<\/span><span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answers<\/span><\/div><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/div>\n    <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n        <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n            <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/152301-find-closest-value-in-array?s_tid=ans_recom_leaf\">Find closest value in array<\/a><\/p>\n            <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                    <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                        <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                            <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/5372183\">\n                                    <img alt=\"Chiranjibi\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"\/responsive_image\/75\/75\/0\/0\/0\/profile\/5372183?s_tid=ans_recom_user\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, '\/responsive_image\/100\/0\/0\/0\/0\/cache\/matlabcentral\/profiles\/profilepic_default.gif');\">\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                            <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/5372183\">Chiranjibi<\/a> on 25 August 2014\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                    <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\">I have two vector(which are time stamps): V = [1375471092848936; 1375473388165900; 1375471320476780; 1375473388947681; 1375473392527002]; N = [1375473384440853; 1375471277856598; 1375473388165900; 1375471322465961; 1375471335206288]; My goal is to find closest time in N with respect to V (i.e. find...<\/p>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta answer-tag-list tags_ans_lp\"><strong>Tags<\/strong>:<a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'vector'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">vector<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'array'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">array<\/a><\/div>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\"><ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\"><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span>4<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span>391<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-feedback feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span>0<\/li><\/ul><\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\"><div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\"><div class=\"answers_meta -is_accepted\" data-accepted-label=\"Accepted Answer\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"1 Accepted Answer, 5 Answers\"><span class=\"answers_meta_count\">6<\/span><span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answers<\/span><\/div><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/div>\n    <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n        <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n            <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/511791-how-to-plot-the-directed-graph-using-nxn-matrix-in-matlab?s_tid=ans_recom_leaf\">how to plot the directed graph using NxN matrix in matlab<\/a><\/p>\n            <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                    <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                        <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                            <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/8175745\">\n                                    <img alt=\"Abdulhakim Alezzi\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"\/responsive_image\/75\/75\/0\/0\/0\/profile\/8175745?s_tid=ans_recom_user\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, '\/responsive_image\/100\/0\/0\/0\/0\/cache\/matlabcentral\/profiles\/profilepic_default.gif');\">\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                            <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/8175745\">Abdulhakim Alezzi<\/a> on 19 March 2020\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                    <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\"> Hi friends , I have a matrix with 30x30 , where the first row and first column representing the nodes just as shown below . 1- I want to plot a directed graph between the nodes using the edges values between the nodes 2- I want to to apply the threshould (thr = 0.2) to plot the the graphs using the...<\/p>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta answer-tag-list tags_ans_lp\"><strong>Tags<\/strong>:<a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'directed graph'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">directed graph<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'graphs'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">graphs<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'graph theory'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">graph theory<\/a><\/div>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\"><ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\"><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span>0<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span>328<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-feedback feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span>0<\/li><\/ul><\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\"><div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\"><div class=\"answers_meta -is_accepted\" data-accepted-label=\"Accepted Answer\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"1 Accepted Answer\"><span class=\"answers_meta_count\">1<\/span><span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answer<\/span><\/div><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/div>\n    <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n        <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n            <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/2184652-dear-all-i-have-the-following-integral-standard-numerical-integration-direct-summation-takes-abo?s_tid=ans_recom_leaf\">Dear all, I have the following integral. Standard numerical integration (direct summation) takes about 40 seconds on a regular PC. Any tricks to reduce this to a few seconds? <\/a><\/p>\n            <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                    <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                        <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                            <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/20266973\">\n                                    <img alt=\"ma Jack\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"\/responsive_image\/75\/75\/0\/0\/0\/profile\/20266973?s_tid=ans_recom_user\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, '\/responsive_image\/100\/0\/0\/0\/0\/cache\/matlabcentral\/profiles\/profilepic_default.gif');\">\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                            <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/20266973\">ma Jack<\/a> on 17 August 2026\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                    <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\">I need to compute the following integral, where bold letters denote matrices. With Ny = 50, all matrices are 100\u00D7100. For stability, I use LU decomposition for log|det(\u00B7)|, discretizing k1 and doing an LU step at each point \u2014 totaling about 40 seconds, which is too slow. But only C(k1) changes with ...<\/p>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta answer-tag-list tags_ans_lp\"><strong>Tags<\/strong>:<a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'numerical integration'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">numerical integration<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'numerical linear algebra'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">numerical linear algebra<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'fast numerical integration'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">fast numerical integration<\/a><\/div>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\"><ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\"><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span>0<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span>165<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-feedback feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span>4<\/li><\/ul><\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\"><div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\"><div class=\"answers_meta -is_accepted\" data-accepted-label=\"Accepted Answer\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"1 Accepted Answer\"><span class=\"answers_meta_count\">1<\/span><span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answer<\/span><\/div><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/div>\n    <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n        <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n            <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/101078-why-do-i-receive-an-error-about-an-invalid-file-installation-key-when-installing-matlab-manually-wit?s_tid=ans_recom_leaf\">Why do I receive an error about an invalid File Installation Key when installing MATLAB manually without the Internet?<\/a><\/p>\n            <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                    <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                        <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                            <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/4622813\">\n                                    <img alt=\"MathWorks Support Team\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"\/responsive_image\/75\/75\/0\/0\/0\/profile\/4622813?s_tid=ans_recom_user\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, '\/responsive_image\/100\/0\/0\/0\/0\/cache\/matlabcentral\/profiles\/profilepic_default.gif');\">\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                            <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/4622813\">MathWorks Support Team<\/a> on 14 January 2010\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                    <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\"> When installing MATLAB manually without the Internet, I provided the File Installation Key provided by the MathWorks. When I enter the File Installation Key the installer tells me that it is invalid. How can I install my MATLAB manually without the Internet?\u00A0 kA0i00000007qbOCAQ 000025941<\/p>\n                    \n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\"><ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\"><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span>12<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span>1130<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-feedback feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span>0<\/li><\/ul><\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\"><div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\"><div class=\"answers_meta -is_accepted\" data-accepted-label=\"Accepted Answer\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"1 Accepted Answer\"><span class=\"answers_meta_count\">1<\/span><span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answer<\/span><\/div><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/div>\n    <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n        <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n            <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/1818995-why-do-i-receive-the-error-this-email-is-not-linked-to-a-license-use-a-different-email-address?s_tid=ans_recom_leaf\">Why do I receive the error &quot;This email is not linked to a license. Use a different email address...&quot; when I try to launch MATLAB?<\/a><\/p>\n            <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                    <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                        <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                            <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/4622813\">\n                                    <img alt=\"MathWorks Support Team\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"\/responsive_image\/75\/75\/0\/0\/0\/profile\/4622813?s_tid=ans_recom_user\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, '\/responsive_image\/100\/0\/0\/0\/0\/cache\/matlabcentral\/profiles\/profilepic_default.gif');\">\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                            <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                                <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"\/matlabcentral\/profile\/authors\/4622813\">MathWorks Support Team<\/a> on 26 September 2022\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                    <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\"> The following error can occur when launching MATLAB. This email is not linked to a license. Use a different email address or go to your MathWorks Account to link a license. After the license is linked, try again. kA03q000001I3WnCAK 000295493<\/p>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta answer-tag-list tags_ans_lp\"><strong>Tags<\/strong>:<a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'online'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">online<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span><a href=\"\/matlabcentral\/answers\/?term=tag:'licensing'&s_tid=ans_lp_tag\" rel=\"nofollow\">licensing<\/a><\/div>\n                    <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\"><ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\"><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span>0<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span>3293<\/li><li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-feedback feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span>0<\/li><\/ul><\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\"><div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\"><div class=\"answers_meta -is_accepted\" data-accepted-label=\"Accepted Answer\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"1 Accepted Answer\"><span class=\"answers_meta_count\">1<\/span><span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answer<\/span><\/div><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/div>\n<\/div>"}],"type":"actions","responseTokens":{"profile.lastViewedEntity":"index","activity.name":"PERS_RECO_MLC-ANSWERS_WW_2026-06","profile.viewedAnswers":"[\"blogs index page\",\"/matlabcentral/cody\",\"/products/matlab-drive.html\",\"/support/bugreports/\",\"/matlabcentral/answers/index/\",\"homepage\",\"/search/user-center\",\"/company/trust-center.html\",\"/company/trust-center/privacy-policy.html\",\"/company/trust-center/piracy.html\"]","profile.ip_address":"99.61.2.250","profile.visitNumber_1":"true","geo.city":"smyrna","activity.id":"667293","profile.Three_impression_Login":"1","experience.name":"Experience B","geo.country":"united states","offer.name":"Offer 1780998743827","activity.decisioningMethod":"server-side","profile.twogroups":"GroupB"},"sourceType":"target"}]}}}